"""Deli Counter 0.251.0 (the factory's roadmap 288): a room holding an objective or loot marker keeps its dressing
off its routes.

The factory's census, reading the dressing over the functional build as the walker's guide does, found seven of its
eight detours over 10 % in objective rooms, each one door-to-marker route lengthened by a carton pile or two.
`reserves_routes` says what keeps off a room's routes -- every floor piece on a corner store's floor, the clusters in
a room holding a marker -- and the shelter pass keeps off them too. The contract's sightlines note stops naming a 1.2
m crossing nothing carries. 51 rooms of 50 specs refurnished, every one a marker room.

What this writes, every target pinned by its hash and refused on a mismatch, nothing written until every file has been
worked out: `agent_contract.json`, `level_design.py` and `test_reserved_routes.py` (anchored hunks); the fifty
refurnished specs, carried whole; the new `test_marker_room_routes.py`; VERSION; the CHANGELOG entry, prepended.
Generated from a proven clone (`patches/dc_marker_routes/gen_dc_marker_routes.py`), dry-run on a fresh clone to the
clone's every byte, a second run refused (`patches/dc_marker_routes/dry_run_*.out.txt`).

    python patches/patch_dc_marker_routes.py
    cd deli_counter && python build.py --all && python -m pytest -q && python check.py
"""
